  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.424708333333333,
      "text": "Imagine two identical digits applying for different jobs in a giant number.",
      "source_sha256": "65ce8f8ff4315a2c69c8da6f948273bfe7fe53571c815d2f119fe8ad32561fe6"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.544708333333333,
      "end": 8.779916666666667,
      "text": "One earns ten times as much as its neighbour!",
      "source_sha256": "e4a3be561b1d869393c490c3bd6c39d650b9be10622b41ed3549bf17d0bbc0d8"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.899916666666666,
      "end": 12.592666666666666,
      "text": "How can the very same digit have such different values?",
      "source_sha256": "e1446475747d8c300555d69c3edd97492d6627edfbc1d79b443dc0ab24b490f1"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.712666666666667,
      "end": 15.536708333333333,
      "text": "Let’s uncover its place-value secret.",
      "source_sha256": "68088845a924af60d3faacc2a2274d773e24635ea1d6273bf36f7dc9b1566e57"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.9,
      "end": 21.324708333333334,
      "text": "Today, we’re learning to explain how a digit’s place changes its value in a whole number.",
      "source_sha256": "be28566579f7722708a053df63c2260a87aa352c27f94ed64d2aa1db26504a63"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.7,
      "end": 25.3345,
      "text": "You’ll be able to name a digit’s place and give its value.",
      "source_sha256": "5c15f3863b9960f8c0627a40632990690ba35f878b944e83dc737fe8af84d0c6"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.7,
      "end": 29.726625,
      "text": "You’ll be able to use a place-value chart to explain a number.",
      "source_sha256": "1bbf2d21a829fcbc6bd8b766e6bdbe25066d4be1382bd93d129987ffb3e6d558"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.1,
      "end": 36.28745833333333,
      "text": "You’ll be able to explain why the same digit is worth ten times as much one place to the left.",
      "source_sha256": "7e0d5566de46146e091aec92fba65a27e443acea506d2c787ea0da695effb70f"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.666666666666664,
      "end": 40.17004166666667,
      "text": "What makes the same digit worth ten times as much?",
      "source_sha256": "0ec4b8e24b896da71ac6e1727df4d8ee544a81effd25a3bf6fd097be162182d4"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.29004166666667,
      "end": 42.02495833333333,
      "text": "Its position does.",
      "source_sha256": "11a43e77ec0d7bb7d4d6d7cc83b232c80d27a0dd0dd18098d172443d1fdacb31"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.144958333333335,
      "end": 47.300666666666665,
      "text": "In our base ten system, ten ones make one ten, and ten tens make one hundred.",
      "source_sha256": "154a122e885342d499402a10e73c2c5db717cec41f6efa6734d1cbdd6695c722"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.42066666666667,
      "end": 51.451625,
      "text": "Each place is ten times the place immediately to its right.",
      "source_sha256": "5d00fe2bbb624e7af4af80721178d0d5f3829823d44f2ba30e95fbb9fe1cc4cb"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.833333333333336,
      "end": 54.084125,
      "text": "Look at the seven in this number.",
      "source_sha256": "32f7f03f26dcbcc119bcc6ee38263f09fa837a0bdf597c10c0b6fda1092e5721"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.204125,
      "end": 57.411125,
      "text": "Before I explain, predict which place it holds.",
      "source_sha256": "2afb9f511927e7449d4510fa2e400e485bf1bc7f3efcad84bd49731c31d03ffa"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.531125,
      "end": 60.17008333333333,
      "text": "Remember to count from ones at the right.",
      "source_sha256": "c73a230483b8b3e8752083106b07e760106cedb1cfef6466f82888f95c0b910f"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.7,
      "end": 66.60045833333334,
      "text": "Look at four hundred and seventy two thousand, six hundred and thirty one.",
      "source_sha256": "63ad4646c1354cc4a62b181eed37d407eaca06539afc2151e64b8c1795932179"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.72045833333334,
      "end": 71.422,
      "text": "Put each digit into its own column, from hundred thousands down to ones.",
      "source_sha256": "2b964ac3604b1f3137fa5aeea850436962044d82b634bd79ad4f2baded7fef59"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.542,
      "end": 74.53675,
      "text": "The seven is in the ten thousands column.",
      "source_sha256": "69f19ef07edfa29aa2da2feef43198494365f35e2ee39f6ccd981bdf93178fb1"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.65675,
      "end": 78.52425,
      "text": "Its value is seventy thousand, not seven thousand.",
      "source_sha256": "c31d082653659326229d71e1e20449213e305c130a5ed27a36fe77138184ca7d"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.9,
      "end": 83.75670833333334,
      "text": "The two stands for two thousand, the six for six hundred, and the three for thirty.",
      "source_sha256": "426fe597c216714e86ee07ffa1c4f94037e427a4956974d2ccdefe9b30758117"
    },
    {
      "start": 83.87670833333334,
      "end": 90.22754166666667,
      "text": "Reading the number in groups helps: four hundred and seventy two thousand, then six hundred and thirty one.",
      "source_sha256": "79fd337e7c160c3cfa7813bdc8080df2c39249da8ce9646e4f16bc69fd2cd740"
    },
    {
      "start": 90.34754166666667,
      "end": 92.466375,
      "text": "Every digit has a job.",
      "source_sha256": "8414f23259fbed28808d74a0459b58ad02ea013224e705266c05feaf1695c64b"
    },
    {
      "start": 92.83333333333333,
      "end": 94.86483333333334,
      "text": "Now look at these two fives.",
      "source_sha256": "00924920152f82a36e4a263ca138c269cccb780a73ca2fe3fa0c05650305bd65"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.98483333333333,
      "end": 97.30658333333334,
      "text": "Which one has the greater value?",
      "source_sha256": "4ca8bbc1e26329f1987ca1a89074e832ba9db1ba4871e520e1a85c8133484042"
    },
    {
      "start": 97.42658333333334,
      "end": 100.011,
      "text": "Point to its column before we compare.",
      "source_sha256": "efa89a9e3e5d8b8ebab7123a968d34e2c7b09feb51f62bd044dde8833673571b"
    },
    {
      "start": 101.53333333333333,
      "end": 105.177,
      "text": "Now compare the two fives in fifty five thousand.",
      "source_sha256": "2dcf75c049b730d92df8d827118b5b11ea5e44961a21863635d369924d97a18d"
    },
    {
      "start": 105.297,
      "end": 108.39291666666666,
      "text": "The first five represents fifty thousand.",
      "source_sha256": "5a8358c55bf20a9d1c0ad84f3168ec9a3e243c25ca94bec5d01d3f3f28d86071"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.51291666666667,
      "end": 111.382875,
      "text": "The second represents five thousand.",
      "source_sha256": "b93c47188e6951c474e86ee0f9c430dc7744267c329e753fdcfe9981adbc6f1a"
    },
    {
      "start": 111.502875,
      "end": 116.811875,
      "text": "Fifty thousand is ten times five thousand, even though the digits look the same.",
      "source_sha256": "4489b9080d62d5570b1191cfc967a5f5dd63c21a1bf3ef07fd12521a4aba8685"
    },
    {
      "start": 117.16666666666667,
      "end": 122.25829166666666,
      "text": "This relationship helps us multiply and divide whole numbers by ten.",
      "source_sha256": "cf08ed689a7173ff42888303d76e15ca2f3ea24bd7b27af9a2847ec66f2c2fea"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.37829166666667,
      "end": 125.85366666666667,
      "text": "Thirty four times ten is three hundred and forty.",
      "source_sha256": "565d1ff710396ff8ecbf07fdb091b3ae9ea0b3f0a8fdc01909eb956756499749"
    },
    {
      "start": 125.97366666666667,
      "end": 129.49466666666666,
      "text": "Each digit takes a place worth ten times as much.",
      "source_sha256": "0553e8cf80b8c2786f3a47d830453014657f19970434fc42858512196f87c89f"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.61466666666666,
      "end": 133.647,
      "text": "Three hundred and forty divided by ten returns thirty four.",
      "source_sha256": "769963356c36a6de3e4f0ecc34cdde9a267d32fccce2eddee2a4b21664d28f05"
    },
    {
      "start": 134.0,
      "end": 138.40033333333332,
      "text": "A common mix-up is saying that the seven here is just worth seven.",
      "source_sha256": "ca2bd633dc800baa6fe37fa3c9b7c0a32ec62d2d9a48fec3a1885e133dd3a8b2"
    },
    {
      "start": 138.52033333333333,
      "end": 142.34220833333333,
      "text": "Seven names the digit, but its column tells us its value.",
      "source_sha256": "3e63b140d1f988da46bcf7354cf7d4173b17a1b02cc05a1aeb69f3a1265b6987"
    },
    {
      "start": 142.46220833333334,
      "end": 147.1915,
      "text": "In the ten-thousands column, it represents seven groups of ten thousand.",
      "source_sha256": "878b63cf42df8635e275dc69ba65cadbeaa2483ccea804c4f8bea3a1c4bdb3e8"
    },
    {
      "start": 147.56666666666666,
      "end": 153.08495833333333,
      "text": "In 583,214, what is the value of the eight?",
      "source_sha256": "39ec599455a90c89929ffc14310bd926b40c9439241f8a23df780ffd0fd9b5cf"
    },
    {
      "start": 158.1,
      "end": 160.754875,
      "text": "The eight is in the ten-thousands place.",
      "source_sha256": "24c3c501d7353eaaa8a2ef34304dd579ff75cb6143b60f3f20cb4c0ad6ec3168"
    },
    {
      "start": 160.874875,
      "end": 163.20908333333333,
      "text": "Its value is eighty thousand.",
      "source_sha256": "88c00764728d9cdeaa07ffaa4716010c4d0d3d7d6df7cf75bb562f290b787b0b"
    },
    {
      "start": 163.56666666666666,
      "end": 168.858375,
      "text": "Try the page example: five hundred and eighty three thousand, two hundred and fourteen.",
      "source_sha256": "7d08edc046b394a0196b30dbedef92b6504247b014bf86967ed1b1bc7a9e8a35"
    },
    {
      "start": 168.978375,
      "end": 173.81095833333333,
      "text": "The eight is in the ten thousands place, so it represents eighty thousand.",
      "source_sha256": "634233ec71ff5a4a827bda79a327d707f980b8b9938d6985961de39f1a045cdc"
    },
    {
      "start": 173.93095833333334,
      "end": 177.49783333333335,
      "text": "Remember: name the place first, then work out the value.",
      "source_sha256": "aba596da1bbca29921160322d0a9dd9eff9764e4a57a040e13f7c780f3ec71f3"
    },
    {
      "start": 177.61783333333332,
      "end": 180.73429166666668,
      "text": "One place left means ten times as much.",
      "source_sha256": "26e73739c2d24f2967f28dcb9966ba0c8fb8fc04e7db82ca6468c9e83aaeabda"
    },
    {
      "start": 181.1,
      "end": 186.36354166666666,
      "text": "Our goal was to explain how a digit’s place changes its value in a whole number.",
      "source_sha256": "d7bf94f0654a9c2a7a4f3cd3da7af921da0b90bb054684da1b5ef28437d27e54"
    },
    {
      "start": 186.48354166666667,
      "end": 192.266,
      "text": "You can now explain your strategy, check the places carefully, and show why your answer makes sense.",
      "source_sha256": "51d819bcb5bf6b50cfc852f9fba23757e88637863135525c30c2cbaa98f9d36f"
    },
    {
      "start": 192.386,
      "end": 196.00079166666666,
      "text": "Choose a number of your own and explain it to someone nearby.",
      "source_sha256": "05b80a6c9824eeffe145f354eb8bc852e3df38e8246550f62ac27d78afd66c1a"
    },
    {
      "start": 196.12079166666666,
      "end": 199.30858333333333,
      "text": "Then try the lesson practice on Math Magic.",
      "source_sha256": "6797a6ee6e7035ba17688f4339fae0dc52cacf162ba5c0e78f9ad335fbaec39c"
    }
  ],
